{
    "background_story": "Marlowe was a brilliant and eccentric scientist who had spent his entire career studying the mysteries of the human digestive system. His colleagues often joked that he was obsessed with bowel movements, but Marlowe didn't mind - he was convinced that the key to unlocking optimal health lay in understanding the intricacies of gut function. Marlowe's own struggles with obstipation, or constipation, had driven him to dedicate his life to finding a solution. Through years of tireless research, he developed a groundbreaking new treatment that used natural fibers and probiotics to regulate the digestive system. Marlowe's discovery revolutionized the field of gastroenterology, earning him accolades and improving the lives of millions. Despite his success, Marlowe remained humble, always crediting his own struggles with obstipation for sparking his passion for research.",
